    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "PIANO HEIST"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                \nWe are excited to announce that we have two incredible, genre-spanning shows that we are offering to you as PAY WHAT YOU CHOOSE, starting at $5 per ticket!!!\nPIANO HEIST: Saturday November 4 at 7:30pmPianists and lifelong friends NICO RHODES and PATRICK COURTIN set off on a divine quest to redeem the keyboard and reinstate its reputation as the greatest instrument of ALL TIME. Armed with the music of the greatest composers of the past 400 years — from Bach to Queen –Nico and Patrick deliver a comedic musical theatrical wonder, full of heartfelt stories, piano history, and a world of musical madness. A very fun show for all ages!\nSTICK&BOW: Friday November 10 at 7:30pmThe trailblazing Montreal duo of Canadian MARIMBA player KRYSTINA MARCOUX & Argentinian CELLIST JUAN SEBASTIAN DELGADO play everything from Beethoven to Sting. Presented in partnership with Debut Atlantic, their stunning music is sprinkled with humour, transforming the listening of familiar works in refreshing and unexpected ways. Audiences will be enthralled with a program that pushes the technical limits of what a marimba and cello can do together. Stick & Bow’s critically-acclaimed debut album Resonance is praised by Toronto’s The WholeNote as “just brilliant” & “totally delightful” and by La Scena Musicale as full of “pleasant surprises.” Don’t miss seeing them live!!!\nTICKETS: \n\nPAY WHAT YOU CHOOSE starting at $5 (including HST)\nRecommended Price for adults: $30\n\nAbout Pay What You Choose: Our mission is to being you world-class live performance, and to make it accessible to all. While the recommended price is $30 for adults, we invite you to enjoy the Pay What You Choose option. We encourage you to bring a friend or neighbour to help spread the joy of live performance!!! \nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian when attending a King’s Theatre event\nClick here for King’s Ticket Exchange policies\n \n            "
      }
    ],
