    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "YOUTH IMPROV WORKSHOP SERIES"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                \n\n\n\nJoin GEORGE CLAIRMONT — actor, writer, director, and improviser — for a fun series of after school workshops to learn how to improvise and have fun!\n\nWorkshops on Tuesdays from 4-6pm, March 19-April 9\n\nPerformance TBA (Show title: “The Instant Soup Opera”)\nParticipants cost for 4 workshops plus a show: $80+hst\n\nAges: 10-15\n\n\nNo script? No problem! Improv is a form of theatre that relies on the actor’s imagination to play along with scenarios made up on the spot! Through a series of fun games and thought exercises, George Clairmont will lead participants to create their own characters and then improvise dialogue and play through a whole universe of situations that revolve around one theme: “soap opera”. We will explore drama, silliness, deep emotions, wacky decisions and questionable choices! Good and evil, cats and dogs, ladies and gentlemen, thieves and robber barons… you can play all of these, just for a start! \n\nFour sessions of 2 hours each, Tuesdays at 4pm at King’s Theatre, registration required.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nKing’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.\nClick here for King’s Ticket Exchange policies\n\n\n\n            "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
