        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "KIM DOOLITTLE &amp; THE DOCTORS"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <p><strong>GET READY FOR A POWERHOUSE NIGHT OF BLUES &amp; ROOTS WITH KIM DOOLITTLE &amp; THE DOCTORS!</strong></p> <p><strong><img class=' wp-image-239978 alignleft' src='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/kim-doolittle-ECBA-300x213.jpg' alt='' width='287' height='204' /> KIM DOOLITTLE: </strong>Singer, Songwriter, Storyteller and Recording Artist, Kim Doolittle is bringing her Show <b>&#8220;50 Years a Singer&#8221; </b>to Kings Theatre.</p> <div>This self proclaimed <b>&#8220;Road Scholar&#8221;</b> will bring a retrospective of her storied musical journey, starting in The Annapolis Valley in the 70&#8217;s that has spanned decades Land and Sea.  She is influenced by Roots, Blues, Gospel and Maritime Folk. Interspersed with her <b>Original Music</b>, she will include an Homage to The Great Girl Singers who inspired her from <b>Janis Joplin, Heart, Bonnie Raitt, Patsy Cline, Joni Mitchell, Bette Midler and Tina Turner</b> to name a few.  She has come full circle to her Maritime Roots and is looking forward to sharing her Muse on the boards of Kings with her band <b>&#8220;The Doctors&#8221;.</b></div> </div> </div> </div> <div></div> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div></div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>THE DOCTORS</strong></p> </div> </div> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div> <div> <p class='tm6 Normal'><strong><span class='tm8'><img class='alignleft wp-image-239980' src='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Bona-photo-258x300.jpg' alt='' width='90' height='105' />Tom Bona: Drums. </span></strong><span class='tm8'>Hi</span><span class='tm7'>s simple, funky, in the pocket grooves and innate feel for what a band needs have earned him a place as one of Canada&#8217;s premier drummers. He is an 7X winner for &#8220;Drummer of the Year&#8221; (Maple Blues) and has played with Myles Goodwyn, Sue Foley, Soulstack, Raoul and The Bigtime, Colin James, The Bourbon Tabernacle Choir, Martha and The Muffins, Damhnait Doyle, Jeff Healey, Morgan Davis and many more. Kim has known him for 3 decades and is thrilled he will be part of &#8220;The Doctors&#8221;. Check him out! </span><strong><u><a href='http://www.tombona.com'><span class='tm9'>www.tombona.com</span></a></u></strong></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p class='tm6 Normal'><strong><span class='tm8'><img class='alignleft wp-image-240088' src='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Donnie-picure-225x300.jpg' alt='' width='90' height='116' />Donnie Donahue: Guitar.</span></strong><span class='tm7'> A truly unique guitar player who literally gets inside of the Music and plays like no other. He is Dynamic, Energetic and delivers a blistering performance that is perfectly subtle until it is time to soar. His history in Country, Punk, Rock and Roll and Rockabilly and as one of the founding members of the Razorbacks make him a perfect foil for Kim whom he has made music with since the 80&#8217;s.  </span></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <div> <p class='tm6 Normal'><strong><span class='tm8'><img class='wp-image-240073 alignleft' src='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/kev_corbett_1440x810__large-e1711469440583-225x300.jpg' alt='' width='90' height='120' /></span></strong><span class='tm7'><strong>Kev Corbett: Bass.</strong> Corbett perfectly marries the classic fingerstyle storytelling Folk upon which he cut his teeth and excels at, with a journeyman bassist/drummer’s quest for groove, a sense of space, and tone.<br /> </span></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> </div> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <div> <div> <p class='tm6 Normal'><strong><span class='tm8'><img class='alignleft wp-image-239982' src='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/Alex-Constable-2-200x300.jpg' alt='' width='90' height='135' />Alex Constable: Sax &amp; Flute</span></strong><span class='tm7'>. Based in Annapolis, NS, he is the Minister at the United Church but also an accomplished Musician in his own right, playing Saxophone, Flute, Guitar and singing with a beautiful, resonant voice. As well as playing with &#8220;The Doctors&#8221;, locally he sings with the Tap Room Growlers. </span></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div></div> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong><img class='alignleft wp-image-240071' src='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2023/12/44190310_2292583194102563_1958047896297275392_o-300x300-1.jpg' alt='' width='90' height='140' />John Ebata: Keyboard.</strong> Respected in all the extended categories of musician, song writer, producer, musical director, arranger and recording engineer. Equally versatile in all musical styles from jazz to world folk songs to rock and R&amp;B. He has become the first choice accompanist of many great singer songwriters and  acclaimed to be of the very top Canadian piano-keyboardists and continues to work with artists from all parts of the world.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>TICKETS</strong></p> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li><strong> Adults $30.00</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $5.00</strong></li> </ul> <p><em>HST additional</em><br /> <a href='https://tickets.kingstheatre.ca/TheatreManager/1/login?membershiptypes'><strong>Royalty Card holders get 10% off</strong></a></p> <p>King’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.</p> <p><strong>Doors open 30 minutes before showtime.<br /> </strong></p> <p><small><a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'><b>Click here for King&#8217;s Ticket Exchange policies</b></a></small></p> </div> <p><iframe title='Kim Doolittle and the Doctors LIVE!' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/QVhuxLEX1gY?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> </div> </div> "
      }
    ],
