        "@value": "KIM DOOLITTLE & THE DOCTORS"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                \n\n\n\nGET READY FOR A POWERHOUSE NIGHT OF BLUES & ROOTS WITH KIM DOOLITTLE & THE DOCTORS!\n KIM DOOLITTLE: Singer, Songwriter, Storyteller and Recording Artist, Kim Doolittle is bringing her Show “50 Years a Singer” to Kings Theatre.\nThis self proclaimed “Road Scholar” will bring a retrospective of her storied musical journey, starting in The Annapolis Valley in the 70’s that has spanned decades Land and Sea.  She is influenced by Roots, Blues, Gospel and Maritime Folk. Interspersed with her Original Music, she will include an Homage to The Great Girl Singers who inspired her from Janis Joplin, Heart, Bonnie Raitt, Patsy Cline, Joni Mitchell, Bette Midler and Tina Turner to name a few.  She has come full circle to her Maritime Roots and is looking forward to sharing her Muse on the boards of Kings with her band “The Doctors”.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nTHE DOCTORS\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTom Bona: Drums. His simple, funky, in the pocket grooves and innate feel for what a band needs have earned him a place as one of Canada’s premier drummers. He is an 7X winner for “Drummer of the Year” (Maple Blues) and has played with Myles Goodwyn, Sue Foley, Soulstack, Raoul and The Bigtime, Colin James, The Bourbon Tabernacle Choir, Martha and The Muffins, Damhnait Doyle, Jeff Healey, Morgan Davis and many more. Kim has known him for 3 decades and is thrilled he will be part of “The Doctors”. Check him out! www.tombona.com\n \nDonnie Donahue: Guitar. A truly unique guitar player who literally gets inside of the Music and plays like no other. He is Dynamic, Energetic and delivers a blistering performance that is perfectly subtle until it is time to soar. His history in Country, Punk, Rock and Roll and Rockabilly and as one of the founding members of the Razorbacks make him a perfect foil for Kim whom he has made music with since the 80’s.  \n \n\n \n\nKev Corbett: Bass. Corbett perfectly marries the classic fingerstyle storytelling Folk upon which he cut his teeth and excels at, with a journeyman bassist/drummer’s quest for groove, a sense of space, and tone.\n\n \n \n\n\n \n\n\nAlex Constable: Sax & Flute. Based in Annapolis, NS, he is the Minister at the United Church but also an accomplished Musician in his own right, playing Saxophone, Flute, Guitar and singing with a beautiful, resonant voice. As well as playing with “The Doctors”, locally he sings with the Tap Room Growlers. \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \nJohn Ebata: Keyboard. Respected in all the extended categories of musician, song writer, producer, musical director, arranger and recording engineer. Equally versatile in all musical styles from jazz to world folk songs to rock and R&B. He has become the first choice accompanist of many great singer songwriters and  acclaimed to be of the very top Canadian piano-keyboardists and continues to work with artists from all parts of the world.\n \nTICKETS\n\n\n\n\n Adults $30.00\nYouth: $5.00\n\nHST additional\nRoyalty Card holders get 10% off\nKing’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.\nDoors open 30 minutes before showtime.\n\nClick here for King’s Ticket Exchange policies\n\n\n\n\n            "
      }
    ],
