    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FODAR: Program One"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Whether you’re new to contemporary dance or a committed fan, you’ll be drawn into Festival of Dance Annapolis Royal’s dazzling MainStage performances. FODAR presents two different programs alternating over 3 days.<br /> PROGRAM ONE runs July 18th (evening) and July 20th (Matinée).<br /> PROGRAM TWO runs evenings on July 19th and 20th.</p> <p><b>PROGRAM ONE:</b></p> <p><em>SOUDAIN L’HIVER DERNIER</em> – a powerful duet by celebrated choreographer James Kudelka and danced by Toronto’s Citadel + Compagnie. Widely acclaimed, this work was an award-winner at the 2007 Edinburgh Fringe Festival.</p> <p><em>SOLO (NOT SOLO) WATER STUDY</em> – Choreographed by Meryem Alaoui (Toronto), this is a lighthearted work where one dancer and one percussionist, attempt to reach an accord between sound and movement.</p> <p><em>BIG TIME MISS</em> – Multi Dora Award-winner Rock Bottom Movement (Toronto) returns to FODAR with a soft World Premiere! Set to an original dancepunk score, this brilliant absurdist production is brought to life through the spectacular dancers of the company and<span class='Apple-converted-space'>  </span>the unbridled imagination of choreographer and Artistic Director Alyssa Martin.</p> <p><b>TICKET PRICES</b><br /> Regular $35<br /> Student $15<br /> Package $50 (A ticket for both Programs, please contact the Box Office)</p> <ul class='tm6 Normal tm11'> <li class='tm12'><span class='tm7'>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</span></li> <li class='tm6 Normal tm12'><span class='tm7'>Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian when attending a King’s Theatre event</span></li> <li class='tm6 Normal tm12'><span class='tm7'>No outside food or drink permitted</span></li> <li class='tm6 Normal tm12'>Tickets are non refundable</li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
