    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FODAR: Program One"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                Whether you’re new to contemporary dance or a committed fan, you’ll be drawn into Festival of Dance Annapolis Royal’s dazzling MainStage performances. FODAR presents two different programs alternating over 3 days.\nPROGRAM ONE runs July 18th (evening) and July 20th (Matinée).\nPROGRAM TWO runs evenings on July 19th and 20th.\nPROGRAM ONE:\nSOUDAIN L’HIVER DERNIER – a powerful duet by celebrated choreographer James Kudelka and danced by Toronto’s Citadel + Compagnie. Widely acclaimed, this work was an award-winner at the 2007 Edinburgh Fringe Festival.\nSOLO (NOT SOLO) WATER STUDY – Choreographed by Meryem Alaoui (Toronto), this is a lighthearted work where one dancer and one percussionist, attempt to reach an accord between sound and movement.\nBIG TIME MISS – Multi Dora Award-winner Rock Bottom Movement (Toronto) returns to FODAR with a soft World Premiere! Set to an original dancepunk score, this brilliant absurdist production is brought to life through the spectacular dancers of the company and  the unbridled imagination of choreographer and Artistic Director Alyssa Martin.\nTICKET PRICES\nRegular $35\nStudent $15\nPackage $50 (A ticket for both Programs, please contact the Box Office)\n\nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian when attending a King’s Theatre event\nNo outside food or drink permitted\nTickets are non refundable\n\n \n \n \n \n \n            "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
