        "@value": "KING'S SHORTS"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                \n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe 15th Festival of 10-Minute Plays will be on stage at King’s Theatre June 21-23. It promises to be a blast, so don’t miss it!\n\n\n\nDirectors include Dany Rousseau, Tracy Summerville, Kelley Pozzolo, AC Silver, Verilea Ellis, Anastacia DesLauriers, Dawn Scott, and Shaeralee McCutcheon. Produced with the assistance of the Annapolis District Drama Group and local cast and crew.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThe eight plays chosen for 2024 are:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nFaded Love by Gene DeJoie, Sherman Oaks, CA\nGodot’s Eternal Taxi Service by JJ Steinfeld, Charlottetown, PEI\nLady Bay by Scott Campbell, Kentville, NS\nNobody Here by Jill Harland, Toronto, ON\nThe Appointment by Bruce Deveau, Amesbury, MA\nThe Future is Ours by Paul Bowman, New Albany, IN\nTo Canterbury They Went  by Dianne Sposito, New York, NY\nWalking the Walk by Seth Freeman, Pacific Palisades, CA\n\n\n \nTICKETS:\n\nAdults: $18\nYouth: $12\n\n\n\n\n\n \nKing’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.\nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian when attending a King’s Theatre event\n\n\n\nClick here for King’s Ticket Exchange policies\n \n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n            "
      }
    ],
