    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div class='moz-text-html' lang='x-unicode'> <p><strong>Sparkle Dance Presents A Multicultural Celebration!</strong></p> <p><em><span class='x4k7w5x x1h91t0o x1h9r5lt x1jfb8zj xv2umb2 x1beo9mf xaigb6o x12ejxvf x3igimt xarpa2k xedcshv x1lytzrv x1t2pt76 x7ja8zs x1qrby5j'><span class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm x14ctfv'><strong>An interactive show for an audience of all ages led by Wendy Goudie. Expect to clap, stomp and dance in your seat while Sparkle Dance campers share their excitement and celebration for world dance!</strong> </span></span></em></p> <p><span class='x4k7w5x x1h91t0o x1h9r5lt x1jfb8zj xv2umb2 x1beo9mf xaigb6o x12ejxvf x3igimt xarpa2k xedcshv x1lytzrv x1t2pt76 x7ja8zs x1qrby5j'><span class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm x14ctfv'>Fourteen youth, ages 6-17 years in age, will be immersing in various dance styles from around the globe, and in just one week, campers will put together an educational show highlighting dance styles such as Bollywood, Bhangra, Greek Belly dance, Spanish Fusion, and Salsa, and more. </span></span></p> <p>This show wraps up a busy camp week with the group creating the show in just 5 days!</p> <p><strong><span class='x4k7w5x x1h91t0o x1h9r5lt x1jfb8zj xv2umb2 x1beo9mf xaigb6o x12ejxvf x3igimt xarpa2k xedcshv x1lytzrv x1t2pt76 x7ja8zs x1qrby5j'><span class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm x14ctfv'><img class='size-medium wp-image-240440 alignleft' src='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2024/07/Diksha-225x300.jpg' alt='' width='225' height='300' />The show also brings special guest Diksha Aggarwal to the King&#8217;s Theatre Stage.  </span></span></strong></p> <p><span class='x4k7w5x x1h91t0o x1h9r5lt x1jfb8zj xv2umb2 x1beo9mf xaigb6o x12ejxvf x3igimt xarpa2k xedcshv x1lytzrv x1t2pt76 x7ja8zs x1qrby5j'><span class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm x14ctfv'>A 27-year-old immigrant from India, Diksha has called Canada home for over eight years. After arriving in 2016 to pursue a childhood educator program,  she now runs her own home daycare, as a permanent resident. </span></span></p> <p><span class='x4k7w5x x1h91t0o x1h9r5lt x1jfb8zj xv2umb2 x1beo9mf xaigb6o x12ejxvf x3igimt xarpa2k xedcshv x1lytzrv x1t2pt76 x7ja8zs x1qrby5j'><span class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm x14ctfv'>Dance has been her passion since grade 4, and she had the privilege of performing in numerous stage shows throughout her school years. She trained in Indian classical dance, specifically Kathak, for two years during grades 11 and 12. Dance is a beloved activity that brings her relaxation, stress relief, confidence, and physical fitness. </span></span></p> <p><span class='x4k7w5x x1h91t0o x1h9r5lt x1jfb8zj xv2umb2 x1beo9mf xaigb6o x12ejxvf x3igimt xarpa2k xedcshv x1lytzrv x1t2pt76 x7ja8zs x1qrby5j'><span class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm x14ctfv'>Diksha was born with a treatable eye disorder called retinal pigmentosa, which progressively affects vision over time. Despite being fully independent when she arrived in Canada, her condition has rapidly progressed in recent years, leaving her unable to read, recognize signs and symbols, or even distinguish faces in a crowd. Her journey thus far has been made possible solely due to the unwavering support of family. Her two younger brothers, mother, and father have been her pillars of strength, providing emotional, financial, and mental support at every step. She is eternally grateful for their love and encouragement. </span></span></p> <p><span class='x4k7w5x x1h91t0o x1h9r5lt x1jfb8zj xv2umb2 x1beo9mf xaigb6o x12ejxvf x3igimt xarpa2k xedcshv x1lytzrv x1t2pt76 x7ja8zs x1qrby5j'><span class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1xmvt09 x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm x14ctfv'>Diksha will be performing a Haryanvi dance from the Indian province of Haryana, as well as an Indian Punjabi dance, which was Choreographed by Ruchika Malik, Director of the Ruchika&#8217;s Rhythm Rockers in Halifax.<br /> </span></span></p> <div id='signature'></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>TICKETS</strong></p> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li><strong> Adults $18.00</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $8.00</strong></li> </ul> <p>King’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.</p> <p><strong>Doors open 30 minutes before showtime.<br /> </strong></p> <p><small><a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'><b>Click here for King&#8217;s Ticket Exchange policies</b></a></small></p> </div> </div> </div> "
      }
