    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/IMG_5720-crop-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/gregory-muszkie-the-greg-show/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "GREGORY MUSZKIE: THE GREG SHOW"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'><strong>King’s Theatre presents ‘The Greg Show’, a night of music, stories and surprises with our own Gregory Muszkie!<br /> </strong></div> </div> </div> </div> <div dir='ltr'></div> <div dir='ltr'>Special guests include Sam Boer, Anita Cazzola, and Maddie Frisby.</div> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'></div> <div dir='ltr'><strong>Gregory Muszkie</strong> is a singer, songwriter, and storyteller who embodies the character of a flawed, naive individual &#8212; ‘Greg’ &#8212; who navigates a crazed modern world. His satirical style combines humour and ennui to bring a unique musical experience to all. Inspired by musics like The Barenaked Ladies, David Bowie, Rufus Wainwright, John Mayer and Stevie Wonder, he embarks on a journey of introspection and becoming.</div> </div> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'>In this solo show, Gregory equips both the piano and guitar to perform original works like ‘Weird Kid’, ‘Plastic’ and ‘One Step From My Heart’.<br /> Themes include: Cautionary storytelling, celebration of the self, love and passion, environmentalism, and the unknown.</div> <div dir='ltr'></div> <div dir='ltr'>Gregory Muszkie is a Graduate of Voice from the university of Regina, Saskatchewan. He is currently the house manager of King’s Theatre, a featured visual artist in the Annapolis Valley, and a big fan of natural sciences. He has been featured in King’s stage productions such as D. Rousseau’s The Rocky Horror: Film and Live Experience, Scrappy Lady Productions’ ‘Dracula’, and King’s Summer Lovin’ Cabaret.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div dir='ltr'></div> <div dir='ltr'><em><strong>Greg’s original music can ONLY be heard at King’s Theatre!</strong></em></div> <p><strong>TICKETS</strong></p> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li><strong> Adults $25.00</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $10.00</strong></li> </ul> <p><em>HST additional</em></p> <p>King’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.</p> <p><strong>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.<br /> </strong></p> <p><small><a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'><b>Click here for King&#8217;s Ticket Exchange policies</b></a></small></p> </div> </div> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> "
      }
    ],
