      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                \n\n\n\n\n\nThe Annapolis District Drama Group presents: DICK WHITTINGTON & HIS CAT, written by Terry R. Francis, directed by Simon Bonnington.\n\n\nFriday December 6 at 7:30pm\nSaturday December 7 at 7:30pm\nSunday December 8 at 3:00pm\n\nTHE CAST\nFAIRY BOWBELLS – Peggy Cheung\nKING RAT – Alex Constable\nDING – Colleen Rowland\nDONG – Corin Rector\nDICK WHITTINGTON – Shaeralee McCutcheon\nRICKI WHITTINGTON / her sister VICTORIA (VICKI) – Mark Kane\nDOUG-FORD, her son – Ryan Hebert\nCHELSEA, the cat – Erik Lehneis\nALDERMAN FITZROVIA FITZWARREN – Tim Wilson\nALICE FITZWARREN, his daughter – Portia Murray\nENSEMBLE:\nFARMHANDS, HUNTING PARTY, LONDONERS, RODENT ARMY, STROLLING PLAYERS\nMICK WHITTINGTON – Jamie Keithline\nNICK WHITTINGTON – Brenda Thompson\nPIG-SWILL PERCY – Liam Winstead\nSHEEP-DIP SALLY – Karen Tomasino\nBULL-HANDLER BELLE – Nancy Anderson\nADGE CUTT, the Rent Collector – Phil Milo\nLORD HECKERSLEY – Wayne Currie\nTHE BUGLER – Lincoln Balser\nHOMELESS HARRIET of HACKNEY – Lynn Walden\nand\nRori Balser\nLogan Divalerio\nAnne McCormick\nCalder McCormick\nHamish Murray\nLeia Rousseau\nDawn Scott\nHannah Smith\nTHE STORY\n\nJoin our hero, Dick Whittington, as he embarks upon an adventure to seek his fortune in Ye Olde London Towne, where “the streets are paved with gold”.\nWith Terry R. Francis’ hilarious and fast-paced script, Dick and his faithful cat must thwart the wicked schemes of King Rat (“Boo! Hiss!”) and his Rodent Army, to save the Londoners from tyranny, and bring ‘happiness ever after’ to his friends and family.\nThis well loved folk-tale has been adapted for Panto many, many times – and Terry’s script rollicks along at a ripping pace, with gags and laughter, and songs and dance galore. Directed by Annapolis District Drama Group stalwart Simon Bonnington, and starring many of your best loved local actors, you are sure to be right royally entertained!\nSo where are ADDG bringing this awesome show to the stage? “Look behind you!” We mean, at King’s Theatre, Annapolis Royal, this December.\nTICKETS:\n\nAdult $20\nYouth $5\n\n \nKing’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.\nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime.\n\nClick here for King’s Ticket Exchange policies\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n            "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
