    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/dick-whittington-his-cat/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "DICK WHITTINGTON &amp; HIS CAT"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><strong>The Annapolis District Drama Group presents: </strong><strong>DICK WHITTINGTON &amp; HIS CAT, written by Terry R. Francis, directed by Simon Bonnington.<br /> </strong></p> <ul> <li>Friday December 6 at 7:30pm</li> <li>Saturday December 7 at 7:30pm</li> <li>Sunday December 8 at 3:00pm</li> </ul> <p><strong>THE CAST</strong></p> <p>FAIRY BOWBELLS – Peggy Cheung<br /> KING RAT – Alex Constable<br /> DING – Colleen Rowland<br /> DONG – Corin Rector<br /> DICK WHITTINGTON – Shaeralee McCutcheon<br /> RICKI WHITTINGTON / her sister VICTORIA (VICKI) – Mark Kane<br /> DOUG-FORD, her son – Ryan Hebert<br /> CHELSEA, the cat – Erik Lehneis<br /> ALDERMAN FITZROVIA FITZWARREN – Tim Wilson<br /> ALICE FITZWARREN, his daughter – Portia Murray</p> <p><strong>ENSEMBLE:</strong><br /> FARMHANDS, HUNTING PARTY, LONDONERS, RODENT ARMY, STROLLING PLAYERS<br /> MICK WHITTINGTON – Jamie Keithline<br /> NICK WHITTINGTON – Brenda Thompson<br /> PIG-SWILL PERCY &#8211; Liam Winstead<br /> SHEEP-DIP SALLY – Karen Tomasino<br /> BULL-HANDLER BELLE – Nancy Anderson<br /> ADGE CUTT, the Rent Collector – Phil Milo<br /> LORD HECKERSLEY – Wayne Currie<br /> THE BUGLER – Lincoln Balser<br /> HOMELESS HARRIET of HACKNEY – Lynn Walden</p> <p><strong><em>and</em></strong><br /> Rori Balser<br /> Logan Divalerio<br /> Anne McCormick<br /> Calder McCormick<br /> Hamish Murray<br /> Leia Rousseau<br /> Dawn Scott<br /> Hannah Smith</p> <p><strong>THE STORY<br /> </strong></p> <p>Join our hero, Dick Whittington, as he embarks upon an adventure to seek his fortune in Ye Olde London Towne, where “the streets are paved with gold”.</p> <p>With Terry R. Francis&#8217; hilarious and fast-paced script, Dick and his faithful cat must thwart the wicked schemes of King Rat (“Boo! Hiss!”) and his Rodent Army, to save the Londoners from tyranny, and bring &#8216;happiness ever after&#8217; to his friends and family.</p> <p>This well loved folk-tale has been adapted for Panto many, many times – and Terry&#8217;s script rollicks along at a ripping pace, with gags and laughter, and songs and dance galore. Directed by Annapolis District Drama Group stalwart Simon Bonnington, and starring many of your best loved local actors, you are sure to be right royally entertained!</p> <p>So where are ADDG bringing this awesome show to the stage? “Look behind you!” We mean, at King&#8217;s Theatre, Annapolis Royal, this December.</p> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adult $20</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth $5</strong></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><em>King’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.</em></p> <p><strong>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.<br /> </strong></p> <p><small><a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'><b>Click here for King’s Ticket Exchange policies</b></a></small></p> <p><em><strong> </strong></em></p> "
      }
    ],
