        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div dir='ltr'> <div class='moz-text-html' lang='x-unicode'> <p><strong>Sparkle Dance returns to the King&#8217;s stage with &#8216;The Power of Love&#8217;, an all new show that will rock your world.</strong></p> <p><strong>Happening Sunday March 2 at 2pm &amp; 6pm.<br /> </strong></p> <p>Experience 70+ children, teens, and adult performers on stage in this highly entertaining community dance show.</p> <p>Led by Wendy Goudie.</p> <div> <p>Experience an unforgettable show of artistry and emotion as the Sparkle Dancers light up the stage with their spectacular new dance show, <em>The Power of Love.  </em>Through captivating choreography and heartfelt performances, <em>The Power of Love</em> delves into the many dimensions of love including:</p> <p>✨ The unconditional love of parents.<br /> ✨ The joy and trust shared between lifelong friends.<br /> ✨ The wisdom and warmth of grandparents and mentors.<br /> ✨ The struggles and lessons dysfunctional relationships.<br /> ✨ The importance of loving yourself and embracing who you are.<br /> ✨ The passion and unity found in the love of dance.</p> <p>With dazzling costumes, breathtaking moves, and soul-stirring music, <em>The Power of Love</em> is a celebration of the bonds that unite us and the emotions that move us. Perfect for audiences of all ages, this show will leave you inspired, uplifted, and remind you of the many ways love shapes our lives.  Whether you come to laugh, cry, or simply be inspired, this show promises something for everyone.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> </div> <ul> <li>Director, Producer and Choreographer: Wendy Goudie</li> <li>Co-Producer, Music and Photography: John Goudie</li> <li>Costumes: Sandra Rector</li> <li>Technical Design: Devin Fraser</li> <li>Energy and Creativity: All the kids!</li> </ul> <p><strong>TICKETS:<br /> </strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adults: $20 for one show/$30 for both shows </strong><em>(please contact the box office at 902-532-7704)</em><strong><br /> </strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $5 for each show<br /> </strong></li> </ul> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <p><strong>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.<br /> </strong></p> </div> <p class='p2'> </div> </div> <p><strong><img class='wp-image-238719 alignleft' src='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2023/02/Wendy-Goudie-300x284.jpg' alt='' width='131' height='124' />Dance Instructor Wendy Goudie</strong> created Sparkle Dance Academy in 2001 in BC Focused on World Dance, this performance school has enjoyed a successful 20+ years in BC, with several locations. The school&#8217;s dancers have performed throughout Canada, and internationally in Greece, Thailand, France, Australia, and India. She has received many acknowledgements such as Okanagan Arts Awards &#8211; Contribution to Dance in 2012, Penticton Arts Council Dance Award 2012 &amp; 2016. Wendy was named Arts Educator of the Year in 2018. Wendy has performed and taught Bollywood Bellydance throughout Canada. In 2018 she completed a month long performance and workshop tour in North India. She was a invited to perform as a finalist on the dance show &#8220;Indian Icon&#8221; in 2019. Now settled in the Annapolis Valley, Nova Scotia, Sparkle Dance has programs on each coast. Wendy is passionate about teaching youth life skills through the art of non-competitive performance.</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><iframe title='Sparkle Power Anthem - Sparkle Dance Academy, Nova Scotia' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/_2p0uJZ0lsM?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> "
