    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/macbeth-e1734099603809.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "2025-2-9T15:00-4:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/endDate": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "2025-2-9T23:59-4:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "MACBETH"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                David Tennant (Doctor Who, Broadchurch) and Cush Jumbo (The Good Wife, Criminal Record) lead a stellar cast in an ‘enthralling’ (★★★★★ Daily Telegraph) new production of Shakespeare’s MACBETH, filmed live at the Donmar Warehouse in London, especially for the big screen.\nUnsettling intimacy and brutal action combine at breakneck speed as Max Webster (Life of Pi, Henry V) directs this tragic tale of love, murder, and nature’s power of renewal. With staging ‘full of wolfish imagination and alarming surprise’ (★★★★★ The Guardian), the immersive 5.1 cinema surround sound places the audience inside the minds of the Macbeths, asking are we ever really responsible for our actions?\n★★★★★ ‘Enthralling…chilling revelation of a production’ The Telegraph\n★★★★★ ‘Full of wolfish imagination and alarming surprise’ The Guardian\n★★★★ ‘David Tennant is simply hypnotic’ The Times\n★★★★ ‘Cush Jumbo … remarkably compelling’ Theatre Weekly\n★★★★ ‘Thrilling’ Time Out\n★★★★ ‘Never for a moment can you tear your attention away’ WhatsOnStage\n★★★★ ‘Oodles of atmosphere’ Daily Mail\n★★★★ ‘A production of galvanising flair and originality’ The Stage\n★★★★ ‘David Tennant and Cush Jumbo are both electrifying’ Gay Times\n★★★★ ‘Max Webster’s ground-breaking production’ London Theatre\nEstimated Run Time 1h 50m\nTICKETS:  $15.95\n\nHST additional\nKing’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.\nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early. \nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian when attending a King’s Theatre event\n\n \n \n            "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/grease-singalong-sockhop/",
    "http://ogp.me/ns#locale": [
