    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p class='tm6'><span class='tm7'>Festival of Dance Annapolis Royal leaps into its second decade with the 11th edition of the Festival. This year FODAR will look to its past and celebrate its future with a diverse group of world class artists and productions which run the spectrum from the quirky and light hearted to the deeply probing and personal.</span></p> <p class='tm6'><strong><span class='tm8'>FODAR 2025 Rundown</span></strong></p> <p><span class='tm7'><strong>MAINSTAGE</strong> shows run with two different programs on alternate days.</span></p> <p class='tm6'><strong><span class='tm8'>PROGRAM ONE (July 17 at 7:30pm &amp; July 19 at 2:00pm)</span></strong></p> <ul class='tm10'> <li class='tm11'><span class='tm7'>A new solo by award-winning Halifax choreographer </span><strong><span class='tm8'>Lydia Zimmer.</span></strong></li> <li class='tm12'><span class='tm7'>Legendary street dancer and choreographer </span><strong><span class='tm8'>Lady C</span></strong><span class='tm7'> performs her Dora Award<br /> winning work Cymatix. This mesmerizing production explores the visual<br /> interpretation of sound and texture and the audio interpretation of movement,<br /> using techniques from Popping, Boogaloo, Animation, Waving, Ticking and other<br /> related Street Dance.</span></li> <li class='tm12'><span class='tm7'>BBoy </span><strong><span class='tm8'>Crazy Smooth</span></strong><span class='tm7'> is one of Canada’s top street dance ambassadors and<br /> founder of the award-winning dance company BBoyism. Now Artistic Director of<br /> the company 10 Gates Dancing, he brings some of Canada’s finest street dancers<br /> to the festival to premiere his new work Boundaries.</span></li> </ul> <p class='tm6'><strong><span class='tm8'>PROGRAM TWO (July 18 &amp; 19 at 7:30pm)</span></strong><span class='tm7'><br /> Two riveting new duets showcase four of Canada’s finest contemporary dancers.</span></p> <ul class='tm10'> <li class='tm11'><strong><span class='tm8'>Miyeko Ferguson</span></strong><span class='tm7'> and </span><strong><span class='tm8'>Jera Wolfe</span></strong><span class='tm7'> perform Jera’s new work Tethered.</span></li> <li class='tm12'><strong><span class='tm8'>Marrin Jessome and Brayden Jamil Cairns</span></strong><span class='tm7'> dance Jumelle(s), choreographed by<br /> Marrin.</span></li> <li class='tm12'><span class='tm7'>The festival presents the revival of a Canadian Modern Dance classic, </span><strong><span class='tm8'>Randy<br /> Glynn&#8217;</span></strong><span class='tm7'>s After Godot. The work made its debut to critical acclaim in 1983. It will<br /> be danced by </span><strong><span class='tm8'>Connor Mitton, Sully Malaeb Proux, Miyeko Ferguson and Randy<br /> Glynn.</span></strong></li> </ul> <p class='tm6'><strong><span class='tm8'>Tickets Prices:</span></strong></p> <ul class='tm10'> <li class='tm13'><span class='tm7'>Regular: $35</span></li> <li class='tm14'><span class='tm7'>Youth: $15</span></li> <li class='tm14'><span class='tm7'>Combo (one ticket for Program One and one ticket for Program Two): $50</span></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><iframe title='Cymatix - Caroline &#039;Lady C&#039; Fraser (Teaser)' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/bgyKJU1L60A?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> "
      }
