    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "FODAR: Program One"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                Festival of Dance Annapolis Royal leaps into its second decade with the 11th edition of the Festival. This year FODAR will look to its past and celebrate its future with a diverse group of world class artists and productions which run the spectrum from the quirky and light hearted to the deeply probing and personal.\nFODAR 2025 Rundown\nMAINSTAGE shows run with two different programs on alternate days.\nPROGRAM ONE (July 17 at 7:30pm & July 19 at 2:00pm)\n\nA new solo by award-winning Halifax choreographer Lydia Zimmer.\nLegendary street dancer and choreographer Lady C performs her Dora Award\nwinning work Cymatix. This mesmerizing production explores the visual\ninterpretation of sound and texture and the audio interpretation of movement,\nusing techniques from Popping, Boogaloo, Animation, Waving, Ticking and other\nrelated Street Dance.\nBBoy Crazy Smooth is one of Canada’s top street dance ambassadors and\nfounder of the award-winning dance company BBoyism. Now Artistic Director of\nthe company 10 Gates Dancing, he brings some of Canada’s finest street dancers\nto the festival to premiere his new work Boundaries.\n\nPROGRAM TWO (July 18 & 19 at 7:30pm)\nTwo riveting new duets showcase four of Canada’s finest contemporary dancers.\n\nMiyeko Ferguson and Jera Wolfe perform Jera’s new work Tethered.\nMarrin Jessome and Brayden Jamil Cairns dance Jumelle(s), choreographed by\nMarrin.\nThe festival presents the revival of a Canadian Modern Dance classic, Randy\nGlynn’s After Godot. The work made its debut to critical acclaim in 1983. It will\nbe danced by Connor Mitton, Sully Malaeb Proux, Miyeko Ferguson and Randy\nGlynn.\n\nTickets Prices:\n\nRegular: $35\nYouth: $15\nCombo (one ticket for Program One and one ticket for Program Two): $50\n\n\n            "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
