    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "KING'S SHORTS"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                \n\n\n\n\n\nThe 16th Festival of 10-Minute Plays will be on stage at King’s Theatre June 20, 21 & 22\n\n\n\n\n\n150 scripts were submitted from around the world, and eight plays were chosen.They are:\n\nEchoes by Bill DiPaolo, Venice, Florida\nMeet at the Restaurant by Brandon Hicks, Saint John, New Brunswick\nRiley versus Riley or How to Write a Play by Johanna Keller, Syracuse, New York\nSweet Gypsy Rose Retirement Home for Burlesque Dancers by Brenda J. Thompson, Perotte, Nova Scotia\nThe Chairwomen by Shawn Samuelson Henry, Davidson, North Carolina\nThe Great After by Ali Joy Richardson, Halifax, Nova Scotia\nThe Prince Who … by Judd Lear Silverman, Denver, Pennsylvania\nWasted Santa by Paul Bowman, New Albany, Indiana\n\n\nThe directors of the eight plays are:\n\nLaura Cooper-Wagner\nVerilea Ellis\nKen Flett\nJamie Keithline\nShaeralee McCutcheon\nWilliam McCormick\nGregory Muszkie\nDawn Scott\n\n\n\n\nThe festival promises to be a blast, so don’t miss it!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTICKETS:\n\nAdults: $20\nYouth: $12\n\n\n\n\n\n \nKing’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.\nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.\nChildren under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian when attending a King’s Theatre event\n\n\n\nClick here for King’s Ticket Exchange policies\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n            "
      }
