  {
    "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/christina-martin/event_241147_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/christina-martin/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/CM-3_Photo-by-Boom-at-Noon-scaled.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/christina-martin/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CHRISTINA MARTIN"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><b>Experience an unforgettable evening of music and storytelling with award-winning artist Christina Martin, <strong>performing with her trio PLUS a string trio, together for one incredible show.</strong><br /> </b></p> <p><b>Inspired by themes of love, loss, healing, and resilience, Christina takes the stage for a performance that blends emotional depth with captivating arrangements.</b></p> <p>Christina Martin is a powerhouse musician, songsmith, and performer hailing from Nova Scotia. Her music dances effortlessly through Pop, Rock, Folk and Americana traditions but stays deftly unchained by any one label, refusing to be pigeon-holed and unafraid to dip into stranger waters. Through it all runs a backbone of raw honesty about the human condition. Be they personal confessions or narrative tales, each song is lovingly crafted, and hits in the heart like a well-thrown punch. With seven studio albums, two live albums, a string of high-profile performances as long as an elephant’s memory and a reputation for transformative liveshows, Christina Martin is a woman on fire.</p> <p>Her brand new album is more sweeping and orchestral than ever before, Christina Martin is going from strength to strength. It’s a fine thing to be a lyrical troubadour with honest lyrics that cut like a razor, and it’s a fine thing to be a performer who can make hips shake and tears flow at the drop of a casual chord. But to hold both in the palm of your hand, as Martin does with such grace, is downright remarkable. Resolute, raw, and infinitely listenable, Christina Martin is like the wind. Her music can be gentle as a kiss upon your cheek, but if you’re caught off guard it can carry you away, and has the power behind it to blow your house down.</p> <p class='tm7'><strong><span class='tm9'>TICKETS</span></strong></p> <ul class='tm11'> <li class='tm12'><strong><span class='tm9'> Adults $40</span></strong></li> <li><strong>Supported $20*</strong></li> <li class='tm13'><strong><span class='tm9'>Youth: $15</span></strong></li> </ul> <p><em><span class='tm14'>HST additional</span></em></p> <p><em>*Supported tickets are a discounted rate for those who need it, made possible thanks to our generous donors.</em></p> <p class='tm7'><span class='tm8'>King’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.</span></p> <p class='tm7'><strong><span class='tm9'>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.<br /> </span></strong></p> <p class='tm7'><strong><u><a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'><span class='tm9'>Click here for King&#8217;s Ticket policies</span></a></u></strong></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><iframe title='Stay with Me - Live Performance - Christina Martin (featuring Ian Bent on Piano)' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/nI900dUmAtc?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> "
      }
    ],
