    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CHRIS RICKETTS &amp; FRIENDS: SEA SHANTY SHOW"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Internationally acclaimed 21st century shanty singer, <strong>Chris Ricketts</strong> of the UK has appeared at top folk and shanty festivals in Germany, Poland, Canada and France. Chris mastered his craft working cruise ships after being a semi-finalist in the BBC Radio 2 young folk awards. Now a touring musician and teacher in secondary schools Chris&#8217; passion for performing allows him to travel the world with his self-penned songs and versions of traditional shanties. With quick-witted comedy, a unique delivery of sea songs and clever songwriting, Ricketts’ live show never fails to satisfy an audience.</p> <p><strong><img class='wp-image-241758 alignleft' src='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/472998367_122194731776224532_135261892710722536_n-276x300.jpg' alt='' width='159' height='173' />Chris has teamed up with Annapolis Royal&#8217;s own LIVIN&#8217; THE DREAM &#8212; Ray Balcom and Maurice LeClair &#8212; rising stars in the East Coast Sea Shanty scene.</strong> Their group<em> Livin&#8217; The Dream</em> have played all over the east this year with even bigger events in 2025. Their high energy filled and comedic banter is extremely entertaining.</p> <div id='i8e4vmc5' class='BaOVQ8 tz5f0K i8e4vmc5 wixui-rich-text' data-testid='richTextElement'> <p><span class='x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs xlh3980 xvmahel x1n0sxbx x1lliihq x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x xudqn12 x3x7a5m x6prxxf xvq8zen xo1l8bm xzsf02u x1yc453h' dir='auto'>He will also be joined by <strong>Tony Trimper, also known as Callehan</strong>. It&#8217;s a night you won&#8217;t want to miss!</span></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong><strong>  </strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>$25 Adult</strong></li> <li><strong>$20 Supported*</strong></li> <li><strong>$10 Youth</strong></li> </ul> </div> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <p><strong><em>HST additional</em></strong></p> <p><em>*Supported tickets are a discounted rate for those who need it, made possible thanks to our generous donors.</em></p> <p>King’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.</p> <p><strong>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</strong></p> </div> </div> </div> <p><small><a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'><b>Click here for King’s Ticket Exchange policies</b></a></small></p> <p><iframe title='CHRIS RICKETTS- LIVE AT KING&#039;S!' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/zQXETOjMzl0?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><iframe title='Songs In The Key Of Sea | Chris Ricketts | Live @TheCarleton |Songwriters From Here And Away' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/rLCpuSsslZo?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> "
      }
    ],
