    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CHRIS RICKETTS & FRIENDS: SEA SHANTY SHOW"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                Internationally acclaimed 21st century shanty singer, Chris Ricketts of the UK has appeared at top folk and shanty festivals in Germany, Poland, Canada and France. Chris mastered his craft working cruise ships after being a semi-finalist in the BBC Radio 2 young folk awards. Now a touring musician and teacher in secondary schools Chris’ passion for performing allows him to travel the world with his self-penned songs and versions of traditional shanties. With quick-witted comedy, a unique delivery of sea songs and clever songwriting, Ricketts’ live show never fails to satisfy an audience.\nChris has teamed up with Annapolis Royal’s own LIVIN’ THE DREAM — Ray Balcom and Maurice LeClair — rising stars in the East Coast Sea Shanty scene. Their group Livin’ The Dream have played all over the east this year with even bigger events in 2025. Their high energy filled and comedic banter is extremely entertaining.\n\nHe will also be joined by Tony Trimper, also known as Callehan. It’s a night you won’t want to miss!\n \nTICKETS:  \n\n$25 Adult\n$20 Supported*\n$10 Youth\n\n\n\n\n\nHST additional\n*Supported tickets are a discounted rate for those who need it, made possible thanks to our generous donors.\nKing’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.\nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.\n\n\n\nClick here for King’s Ticket Exchange policies\n\n \n\n            "
      }
    ],
