    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Shiny Happy People – A Tribute to R.E.M."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div class='xdj266r x11i5rnm xat24cr x1mh8g0r x1vvkbs x126k92a'> <div dir='auto'>King’s Theatre is pleased to present extraordinary Valley musicians <strong>Jeff Hennessy, Nicholas D’Amato, Noah Scanlan, and Alec Bloch </strong>in an authentic tribute to R.E.M.! Special guests include <strong>Sarah Pound</strong> on vocals,  and <strong>Jolene Buchholz</strong> on oboe.</div> </div> <div dir='auto'></div> <div dir='auto'><strong>SHINY HAPPY PEOPLE</strong> is a gorgeous tribute to R.E.M. that will please both die hard fans and those who only know the hits. Intricate guitar parts, ghostly vocals, driving melodic bass lines, weird and wonderful lyrics. You won’t want to miss this special show!!!</div> <div dir='auto'></div> <div dir='auto'><strong>About R.E.M:</strong> What do Nirvana, Peal Jam, Radiohead, and Coldplay have in common? All cite the band <b>R.E.M.</b> as a formative influence. Originally from Athens, Georgia, R.E.M.’s debut album <i>Murmur</i> was hailed by <i>Rolling Stone Magazine</i> as the #1 album of 1983 (#2 was Michael Jackson’s <i>Thriller</i>). They would go on to achieve worldwide fame with their iconic albums <i>Out of Time</i> and <i>Automatic for the People</i>.</div> <p class='tm7'><strong><span class='tm9'>TICKETS</span></strong></p> <ul class='tm11'> <li class='tm12'><strong><span class='tm9'> Adults $30.00</span></strong></li> <li><strong>Supported $20 </strong></li> <li class='tm13'><strong><span class='tm9'>Youth: $5.00</span></strong></li> </ul> <p><em><span class='tm14'>HST additional</span></em></p> <p class='tm7'><span class='tm8'>King’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.</span></p> <p class='tm7'><strong><span class='tm9'>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.<br /> </span></strong></p> <p class='tm7'><strong><u><a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'><span class='tm9'>Click here for King&#8217;s Ticket policies</span></a></u></strong></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> "
      }
    ],
