    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Shiny Happy People – A Tribute to R.E.M."
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                \nKing’s Theatre is pleased to present extraordinary Valley musicians Jeff Hennessy, Nicholas D’Amato, Noah Scanlan, and Alec Bloch in an authentic tribute to R.E.M.! Special guests include Sarah Pound on vocals,  and Jolene Buchholz on oboe.\n\n\nSHINY HAPPY PEOPLE is a gorgeous tribute to R.E.M. that will please both die hard fans and those who only know the hits. Intricate guitar parts, ghostly vocals, driving melodic bass lines, weird and wonderful lyrics. You won’t want to miss this special show!!!\n\nAbout R.E.M: What do Nirvana, Peal Jam, Radiohead, and Coldplay have in common? All cite the band R.E.M. as a formative influence. Originally from Athens, Georgia, R.E.M.’s debut album Murmur was hailed by Rolling Stone Magazine as the #1 album of 1983 (#2 was Michael Jackson’s Thriller). They would go on to achieve worldwide fame with their iconic albums Out of Time and Automatic for the People.\nTICKETS\n\n Adults $30.00\nSupported $20 \nYouth: $5.00\n\nHST additional\nKing’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.\nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime.\n\nClick here for King’s Ticket policies\n \n            "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
