    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div id='comp-kx969csw3' class='KcpHeO tz5f0K comp-kx969csw3 wixui-rich-text' data-testid='richTextElement'> <div class='elementor-column elementor-col-33 elementor-inner-column elementor-element elementor-element-188a402' data-id='188a402' data-element_type='column'> <div class='elementor-column-wrap elementor-element-populated'> <div class='elementor-widget-wrap'> <div class='elementor-element elementor-element-db5b06d elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor' data-id='db5b06d' data-element_type='widget' data-widget_type='text-editor.default'> <div class='elementor-widget-container'> <p><strong>The Annapolis District Drama Group presents </strong><strong>CHARLOTTE&#8217;S WEB</strong></p> <p><strong>Adapted by Joseph Robinette from the book by E.B. White</strong></p> <p><strong>Directed by Shaeralee McCutcheon</strong></p> <ul> <li>Friday December 5 at 7:00pm</li> <li>Saturday December 6 at 7:00pm</li> <li>Sunday December 7 at 3:00pm</li> </ul> <div class='elementToProof'></div> <div class='elementToProof'><i>Step into the magical world of Charlotte’s Web, the heartwarming tale of friendship, kindness, and the extraordinary power of words. This enchanting stage adaptation brings to life all the unforgettable characters from E.B. White’s timeless classic — Wilbur, the radiant young pig; Fern, the girl who fights to save him; and Charlotte, the beautiful and gentle spider whose words spun in her web changes everything.</i></div> <div></div> <div class='elementToProof'><i>As the seasons turn on Zuckerman’s farm, audiences of all ages will be swept up in a story that celebrates loyalty, hope, and the beauty of the everyday. With its mix of humour, tenderness, and a touch of farmyard charm, Charlotte’s Web is a theatrical experience the whole family will treasure.</i></div> <div></div> <div class='elementToProof'> <div class='elementor-widget-container'> <div class='elementToProof'><i>Join us at King’s Theatre for this beloved tale spun with heart and magic!</i></div> </div> <div> <div></div> <div><strong>CAST</strong></div> <div class='elementToProof'>Fern &#8211; Bella Carver</div> <div class='elementToProof'>John Arable &#8211; Alex Constable</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Martha Arable &#8211; Eloise Mailman</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Avery &#8211; Erik Lehneis</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Homer Zuckerman &#8211; Pierce Ivan</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Edith Zuckerman &#8211; AC Silver</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Lurvy &#8211; Madison Fountain</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Wilbur &#8211; Felicity Berryman</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Templeton &#8211; Eva Carver</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Charlotte &#8211; Christine Connolly</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Goose &#8211; Diane Sokoloski</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Gander &#8211; Mark Kane</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Sheep &#8211; Julie Hebert</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Lamb &#8211; Calder McCormick</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Chorus Member 1 &#8211; Portia Murray</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Chorus Member 2 &#8211; Willa Lauzon</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Chorus Member 3 &#8211; Mackenzie Beaton</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Reporter/Announcer &#8211; Kate Silver</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Photographer/Fairgoer &#8211; Connie Rouse</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Spectator 1/Spider 1 &#8211; Starsha McCue</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Spectator 2/Spider 2 &#8211; Pippa Ewer</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Fairgoer 1/Spider 3 &#8211; Declan Trefry</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Fairgoer 2 &#8211; Liam Winstead</div> <div class='elementToProof'>Fairgoer 3 &#8211; Shaeralee McCutcheon</div> </div> </div> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adult $20</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth $5</strong></li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><em>King’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.</em></p> <p><strong>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.<br /> </strong></p> <p><small><a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'><b>Click here for King’s Ticket Exchange policies</b></a></small></p> </div> <p><iframe title='&quot;Charlotte&#039;s Web&quot; - ADDG - In A World...' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/45u9cijBWG0?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> "
      }
