    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/Charlotte.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "2025-12-7T15:00-4:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/endDate": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "2025-12-7T23:59-4:00"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CHARLOTTE'S WEB"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                \n\n\n\n\n\nThe Annapolis District Drama Group presents CHARLOTTE’S WEB\nAdapted by Joseph Robinette from the book by E.B. White\nDirected by Shaeralee McCutcheon\n\nFriday December 5 at 7:00pm\nSaturday December 6 at 7:00pm\nSunday December 7 at 3:00pm\n\n\nStep into the magical world of Charlotte’s Web, the heartwarming tale of friendship, kindness, and the extraordinary power of words. This enchanting stage adaptation brings to life all the unforgettable characters from E.B. White’s timeless classic — Wilbur, the radiant young pig; Fern, the girl who fights to save him; and Charlotte, the beautiful and gentle spider whose words spun in her web changes everything.\n\nAs the seasons turn on Zuckerman’s farm, audiences of all ages will be swept up in a story that celebrates loyalty, hope, and the beauty of the everyday. With its mix of humour, tenderness, and a touch of farmyard charm, Charlotte’s Web is a theatrical experience the whole family will treasure.\n\nJoin us at King’s Theatre for this beloved tale spun with heart and magic!\n\n\n\nCAST\nFern – Bella Carver\nJohn Arable – Alex Constable\nMartha Arable – Eloise Mailman\nAvery – Erik Lehneis\nHomer Zuckerman – Pierce Ivan\nEdith Zuckerman – AC Silver\nLurvy – Madison Fountain\nWilbur – Felicity Berryman\nTempleton – Eva Carver\nCharlotte – Christine Connolly\nGoose – Diane Sokoloski\nGander – Mark Kane\nSheep – Julie Hebert\nLamb – Calder McCormick\nChorus Member 1 – Portia Murray\nChorus Member 2 – Willa Lauzon\nChorus Member 3 – Mackenzie Beaton\nReporter/Announcer – Kate Silver\nPhotographer/Fairgoer – Connie Rouse\nSpectator 1/Spider 1 – Starsha McCue\nSpectator 2/Spider 2 – Pippa Ewer\nFairgoer 1/Spider 3 – Declan Trefry\nFairgoer 2 – Liam Winstead\nFairgoer 3 – Shaeralee McCutcheon\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nTICKETS:\n\nAdult $20\nYouth $5\n\nKing’s Theatre is committed to making live performances accessible to all audiences. If cost is a barrier please contact our Box Office for Bursary Tickets: boxoffice@kingstheatre.ca or 902-532-7704.\nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime.\n\nClick here for King’s Ticket Exchange policies\n\n\n\n\n\n\n            "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@id": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ]
  },
