    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "JENN GRANT"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\n                The JUNO-nominated/multiple ECMA award-winning artist from Halifax returns to King’s Theatre with her multi-instrumentalist husband Daniel Ledwell and bassist Kyle Cunjak for an intimate show that includes both originals and Holiday tunes, interspersed with Jenn’s unique sense of humour and irresistible charm. We can’t wait!\nJenn Grant’s music is deeply empathetic and generous of heart, so of course one day she would invite the whole country to make it with her.\nChampagne Problems, her eighth album and first in the producer’s chair alongside partner Daniel Ledwell, gathers 13 musicians from coast to territory to coast in a series of collaborative Canadian magic tricks spun into classic country, lost disco hits, and ruminative folk fables.\n“Grant’s gorgeous voice swoops and soars across shimmering pop anthems, folk gems, and sunset ballads” — CBC\n“Aural Equivalent of a Warm Embrace” — Pop Matters\n\nTICKETS\nAdults $40\nSupported $20\nYouth: $15\nHST additional\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDoors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.\nKing’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.\nTickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.\nAll persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.\nOutside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.\nFor more information about Theatre policies, click here.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n            "
      }
    ],
