  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242280_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/theresa-malenfant-kim-doolittle/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/blues-2.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "THERESA MALENFANT &amp; KIM DOOLITTLE"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><strong>Get ready for a big night of UNPLUGGED, LOW DOWN DIRTY BLUES with <b>Theresa Malenfant &amp; Scott Medfordand Kim Doolittle &amp; John Ebata</b></strong></p> <p><b>Theresa Malenfant &amp; Scott Medford </b></p> <p>ECMA winner <strong>Theresa Malenfant</strong> and renowned guitarist <strong>Scott Medford</strong> have become one of the most popular blues duo acts in the Atlantic Provinces. They have been performing together in a band for years, but decided to work as a duo only 6 years ago. In that short time they managed to win second place in an International Blues Challenge (IBC) held in Memphis Tennessee.</p> <p><b>Kim Doolittle &amp; John Ebata</b></p> <p class='tm6'><span class='tm7'><strong>Kim Dootlittle</strong> is an Original Artist born in rural Nova Scotia and did her first paid gig as a child. She was a fixture in the Toronto Music Scene for many years playing Festivals and Events, competed in the International Blues Challenge in 2016 and 2020 &amp; has shared the stage with Jeff Healey, Downchild Blues Band, Suzie Vinnick, Ken Whiteley and many more. She’s travelled the Globe with her Guitar in hand and feels like a Road Scholar —sharing her Muse through song and will be dropping her 10</span><sup><span class='tm7'>th</span></sup><span class='tm7'> album in 2026.</span></p> <p><strong>John Ebata</strong> is respected in all the extended categories of musician, song writer, producer, musical director, arranger and recording engineer. Equally versatile in all musical styles from jazz to world folk songs to rock and R&amp;B, he has become the first choice accompanist of many great singer songwriters and  acclaimed to be of the very top Canadian piano-keyboardists and continues to work with artists from all parts of the world.</p> <div id='i8e4vmc5' class='BaOVQ8 tz5f0K i8e4vmc5 wixui-rich-text' data-testid='richTextElement'> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong><strong>  </strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adults: $35</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $10</strong></li> <li>HST additional</li> </ul> </div> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><iframe title='Theresa Malenfant &amp; The Instigators - (Mama) He Treats Your Daughter Mean -Smokin&#039; BluesFest 5' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/fzFdfKiRDrQ?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> <p><iframe title='Kim Doolittle &amp; The Doctors - ECMA Showcase- Natural Born Woman-(original song)' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/eEK8yaZxMUo?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> "
      }
