  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242205_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/thalea-string-quartet/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/Screenshot-2025-10-17-at-11.55.30-AM.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "THALEA STRING QUARTET"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p class=''>“<em>Thalea never failed to deliver a stirring performance</em>” &#8211; Calgary Herald</p> <p class=''>The Thalea String Quartet brings their signature vibrancy and emotional commitment to dynamic performances that reflect the past, present, and the future of the string quartet repertoire while celebrating diverse musical traditions from around the world. Fueled by the belief that chamber music is a powerful force for building community and human connection, the Thalea String Quartet has performed across North America, Europe, and China, and has appeared at the Kennedy Center, Massey Hall, and Weill Hall at Carnegie Hall. They have shared the stage with luminaries of the chamber music world, including members of the Emerson, Brentano, and St. Lawrence String Quartets, and they have performed alongside celebrated artists including Pulitzer Prize-winning composer Caroline Shaw, violist Lawrence Power, acclaimed Canadian band BADBADNOTGOOD, Detroit hip hop icon Mahogany Jones, and visionary R+B artist Charlotte Day Wilson.</p> <p class=''>Committed to shaping and contributing to the future of the string quartet repertoire, the Thalea String Quartet has premiered dozens of new works and has collaborated on new commissions with composers including Osvaldo Golijov, Paola Prestini, Anthony R. Green, Akshaya Avril Tucker, and Tanner Porter.</p> <div id='i8e4vmc5' class='BaOVQ8 tz5f0K i8e4vmc5 wixui-rich-text' data-testid='richTextElement'> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong><strong>  </strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adults: $45 </strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $10</strong></li> <li>HST additional</li> </ul> </div> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><iframe title='Caroline Shaw - Valencia' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/nGeUJrSqqCA?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><iframe title='Joseph Haydn - String Quartet in D major (&quot;The Lark&quot;), Op. 64, No. 5: ii. Adagio cantabile' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/3U5XvLvYjOA?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> "
      }
    ],
