  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242332_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/joyride-2/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/560760123_847025234551680_14536995223351450_n-copy.jpeg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "JOYRIDE"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<h5><strong>Buckle up for JoyRide, a duo that is a fast-paced, multi-instrumental thrill-ride of jazz, ragtime, Latin, klezmer, Celtic, bebop, blues and more!</strong></h5> <p><strong>Colin Maier (oboe, saw, vocals, from Quartetto Gelato) &amp; Mark Camilleri (pianist and music director for The Tenors) are <i>JoyRide</i>.</strong> Their mastery and versatility in a smorgasbord of styles has Colin switching gears between oboe, voice, pennywhistle and even the musical saw  in a high-energy romp that shows off their taste for fun.</p> <p>From “<em>Minnie the Moocher</em>”, to “<em>Air on a Blue String</em>” (a nod to JS Bach), to Chick Corea’s “<em>Spain</em>” and Piazzolla’s heartrending “<em>Tanti Anni Prima</em>”, they pepper their show with hilarious anecdotes and have a blast playing “Stump the Chump” where Mark creates a new song on the spot from random notes provided by members of the audience.</p> <p>“<em>Ridiculous, virtuosic, outside-the-box fun … It takes a lot of nerve to make music as amusing as JoyRide</em>” &#8212; (New York Music Daily)</p> <p>“<em>The audience was enthralled and dizzy with these supermen of music!</em>” &#8212; Eden Mills Community Club.</p> <p>Whether you’re a jazz fan, a classical fan, or a true musical adventurer, you’re guaranteed to enjoy these two virtuosos taking the wheel.  Hit the gas to catch Joyride!</p> <p><strong>TICKETS: </strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>$35 Adults</strong></li> <li><strong>$15 Youth<br /> </strong></li> </ul> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <p><em>HST additional</em></p> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> </div> </div> </div> <div> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'>  </div> </div> </div> </div> "
      }
    ],
