  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242474_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/next-gen-theatre-workshop-19/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/next-gen-banner-1-scaled.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "NEXT GEN THEATRE WORKSHOP"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p>Are you a young person wanting to explore the magical world of theatre? <span class='xv78j7m' spellcheck='false'>THE NEXT GEN THEATRE WORKSHOPS</span> are here!!! <strong>A series of FREE workshops for youth aged 8-17 who are interested in learning all about Theatre — both on stage and backstage.</strong></p> <p><strong>The workshops will take place every Tuesday for 5:30-7:30pm, January 13 to June 2, on the King’s Theatre stage.</strong> While participation in ALL workshops is not mandatory, it is highly recommended as they will all be interconnected. Space is limited, so register today.</p> <p>Participants will learn theatre skills, self confidence, and how to work together in ensemble. Each workshop will focus on a different area of theatre. Topics to be covered include Acting, Story Telling, Improvisation, Directing, Movement, Voice, Production, Stage Tech, and so much more!</p> <p><strong>The workshop series will conclude with a SHOWCASE PERFORMANCE at King’s Theatre on June 13.</strong></p> <p><em>Presented by King’s Theatre in partnership with <span class='xv78j7m' spellcheck='false'>Young Company Productions Association</span> with support from the <span class='xv78j7m' spellcheck='false'>Canada Post</span> Community Foundation.</em></p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> "
      }
    ],
