  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242338_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/the-baby-tyler-show/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/snafu-baby-tyler-show-puppet-show-ingrid-hansen-photographer-helene-cyr11-puppetry-in-victoria.webp"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "EPIDERMIS CIRCUS: THE WEIRDEST PUPPET SHOW YOU&#039;VE EVER SEEN"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div id='item-62e01b9b77c6355ecaa95034' class='sqs-layout sqs-grid-12 columns-12' data-layout-label='Post Body' data-type='item' data-updated-on='1658854556125'> <div id='yui_3_17_2_1_1763739098427_281' class='row sqs-row'> <div id='yui_3_17_2_1_1763739098427_280' class='col sqs-col-12 span-12'> <div id='block-0c7569a975872279d4b7' class='sqs-block html-block sqs-block-html' data-block-type='2' data-border-radii='{&quot;topLeft&quot;:{&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0},&quot;topRight&quot;:{&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0},&quot;bottomLeft&quot;:{&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0},&quot;bottomRight&quot;:{&quot;unit&quot;:&quot;px&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:0.0}}' data-sqsp-block='text'> <div class='sqs-block-content'> <div class='sqs-html-content' data-sqsp-text-block-content=''> <p class=''>This is one of the most surprising shows you&#8217;ll ever see, masterfully performed by puppeteer Ingrid Hansen (Fraggle Rock, Sesame Workshop.) When her fingers move, they instantly come to life. She needs nothing more than a little inspiration to invent comical characters: a mischievous baby, an endearing shark, a clementine doing a striptease&#8230; With the help of cameras and mirrors, her enchanting, inventive, and unbridled little world is projected onto a giant screen. A surreal, funny, and breathtaking universe.</p> <p class=''>SPICY, <strong>FOR AGE 14+.</strong></p> <p class=''><strong>Techniques</strong>: Hand puppetry, projections, mirror effects, illusions, and objects</p> <ul> <li>“Utterly magical, insanely inventive, wickedly funny, BEAUTIFULLY TWISTED, and occasionally erotic! Imagine Shari Lewis possessed by David Lynch” — Winnipeg Free Press ★★★★★</li> <li>“Surpassing the world of the weird, the zany antics of Epidermis Circus live in a universe of absolutely absurd. ” — CRITIC’S CHOICE NYC ★★★★★ Jaycie Buben, All About Solo NY</li> <li>“Hansen turns anything and everything into a puppet and makes it funny. A MUST-SEE!” — FringeReviews.com</li> <li>“GENIUS PHYSICAL COMEDY!” — Entertainment World.</li> <li>“Immensely funny, creative, uproarious and surprising&#8230;Her physicality is impeccable.” — The Star Phoenix</li> <li>“An amazingly versatile physical comedian with a knack for bringing inanimate objects to life.” — The Montreal Gazette​</li> </ul> <p><strong>Produced by</strong> SNAFU for Age 14+<br /> <strong>Performed by</strong> <em>Fraggle Rock</em> Puppeteer Ingrid Hansen<br /> <strong>Co-Created &amp; Directed by</strong> <em>Ride the Cyclone</em> director Britt Small<br /> <strong>Costume by</strong> JIMBO the Drag Clown <em>(Winner RuPaul’s Drag Race)</em></p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>TICKETS: </strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>$30 Adults</strong></li> <li><strong>$15 Youth<br /> </strong></li> </ul> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <p><em>HST additional</em></p> <p><em><strong>Content Warning:</strong> Epidermis Circus</em> includes cartoonish sexual content, curse words, and puppet suicide.<br /> There are moments of dark lighting, loud music, and surprises.</p> <p>Recommended for Audiences age 14+.</p> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <div> <p class='tm6'><span class='tm7'><strong>ABOUT THE ARTIST:</strong> Hot off a tour to the most prestigious puppet festival in Montreal, Danish-Canadian puppeteer Ingrid Hansen tours her spicy puppetry cabaret after shooting 2 seasons of Fraggle Rock with the Jim Henson Company. She spent a year traipsing through Brooklyn’s parks puppeteering a big orange monster on Sesame’s new Emmy-Award-Winning series ‘Helpsters,’ alongside human actors Andrea Martin, John Oliver, Terry Crews, and Margaret Cho. At home in Victoria, Canada, Ingrid also co-creates puppet theatre with the “big kids” inside federal prisons.</span></p> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </li> </ul> </div> </div> <div> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'>  </div> </div> </div> </div> "
      }
    ],
