  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242342_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/the-spinney-brothers/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/661013-spinney01.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "THE SPINNEY BROTHERS"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p class=''>From the Annapolis Valley of Nova Scotia, brothers Allan Spinney (on guitar and vocals) and Rick Spinney (on banjo and vocals) debuted their band in 1991. Known as Canada’s International Bluegrass Band, they featured a tight brother duet vocal style that was immediately recognized for its energetic and distinctive sound. They went on to release 12 albums, including four very successful releases on Mountain Fever Records. These Mountain Fever recordings played a large role in the world wide recognition that would follow.</p> <p class=''>The brothers have charted four number one hits, countless awards at the Eastern Canadian Bluegrass Music Awards, as well as nominations for three IBMA Awards, including Emerging Artist and Song of the Year. Live performances included such prestigious stages as Bill Monroe’s Bean Blossom Festival, Ralph Stanley’s Hills of Home Festival, Nashville’s Station Inn, and MerleFest, to name a few.</p> <p class=''>The Spinney Brothers always strive to put on an energetic and heart felt performance. Drawing on countless hit songs, fan interaction and a general connection through the music, be prepared to be entertained by Rick and Allan, The Spinney Brothers.</p> <p class='tm7'><strong><span class='tm9'>TICKETS</span></strong></p> <ul class='tm11'> <li class='tm12'><strong><span class='tm9'> Adults $40.00</span></strong></li> <li class='tm13'><strong><span class='tm9'>Youth: $15.00</span></strong></li> </ul> <p><em><span class='tm14'>HST additional</span></em></p> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p class='tm7'> <p><iframe title='The Spinney Brothers: Gravel In Your Shoes | Jubilee | KET' width='1080' height='608' src='https://www.youtube.com/embed/UzmxRtLuIBM?feature=oembed'  allow='accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share' referrerpolicy='strict-origin-when-cross-origin' allowfullscreen></iframe></p> "
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2026-7-11T19:30-4::00"
