  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242352_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/constellations/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/Screenshot-2025-11-21-at-5.42.45-PM.png"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "CONSTELLATIONS"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<div id='comp-ly4fq7k3' class='Z_l5lU ku3DBC zQ9jDz qvSjx3 Vq6kJx comp-ly4fq7k3 wixui-rich-text' data-testid='richTextElement'> <p><em>After a stunning run at <span class='wixui-rich-text__text'>Tarragon Theatre in Toronto last Summer, Icarus Theatre&#8217;s CONSTELLATIONS comes to Annapolis Royal.</span></em></p> <p><strong>CONSTELLATIONS: A PLAY BY NICK PAYNE</strong></p> <p class='font_6 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'>One relationship. Infinite possibilities.<br class='wixui-rich-text__text' /><br class='wixui-rich-text__text' />In the beginning Marianne and Roland meet at a party. They go for a drink, or perhaps they don&#8217;t. They fall madly in love and start dating, but eventually they break up. After a chance encounter in a supermarket they get back together, or maybe they run into each other and Marianne reveals that she&#8217;s now engaged to someone else and that&#8217;s that. Or perhaps Roland is engaged. Maybe they get married, or maybe their time together will be tragically short.<br class='wixui-rich-text__text' /><br class='wixui-rich-text__text' />Nick Payne&#8217;s Constellations is a play about free will and friendship; it&#8217;s also about quantum multiverse theory, love, and honey.</span></p> </div> <p class='font_6 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'>&#8220;[Goncharov and Corcoran&#8217;s] chemistry and dynamic are brilliantly caustic, cute, and electric.&#8221;</span> &#8212; FrontMezzJunkies</p> <p><strong>Cast and Crew</strong></p> <ul> <li>CONNOR BRIGGS: Director/Producer</li> <li>ANTHONY GONCHAROV: Roland/Co-Producer</li> <li>EMILY ANNE CORCORAN: Marianne/Co-Producer</li> <li>MONIQUE DANIELLE: Stage Manager<br /> AMIT KUMAR: Sound Design</li> <li>LIDIA FOOTE: Lighting Design</li> </ul> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adults: $35</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $15 (Under 18)</strong></li> <li>HST additional</li> </ul> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li style='list-style-type: none;'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime. Please arrive early.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </li> </ul> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> "
      }
    ],
