  {
    "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/event_242475_0",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/Event"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/new-events/the-final-recordings-of-an-almost-extinct-bird/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://www.kingstheatre.ca/kingweb/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/494302742_1267454042052547_2244218746655134312_n.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://kingstheatre.ca/events/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Final Recordings of an Almost Extinct Bird"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<p><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>“Final Recordings” is where TEDTalk, sob story, and cottagecore collide.</span></span></p> <p class='font_8 wixui-rich-text__text'><em><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Fred has a lot on his mind. The origins of the universe, for starters. The fabric of space-time, too. The formation of the Earth, plate tectonics, the fossil record, gravitational waves, dark matter, winding valley roads, campfires, pottery cafes—the list goes on and on. There’s also the matter of the giant salty egg, the man in the comfy blue chair, and the burning question: “Is this good? What I’m doing? With my time?”</span></span></em></p> <p class='font_8 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Performed and sound designed by Stewart Legere with projections by Christian Ludwig Hansen, lighting by Jessica Lewis, costumes, set and props designed by Leesa Hamilton, and directed by Ben Stone.</span></span></p> <p><strong>Runtime: 90 minutes, no intermission.</strong></p> <div id='comp-m9u4mxux3' class='Z_l5lU ku3DBC zQ9jDz qvSjx3 Vq6kJx comp-m9u4mxux3 wixui-rich-text' data-testid='richTextElement'> <p class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><strong><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'>Zuppa: </span></strong><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'>Based in Kjipuktuk / Halifax, we aim to make extraordinary experiences that provoke the consideration of new perspectives and ideas and thrive on the play between the imagined and the real. With each project we attempt to do something we don’t know how to do and work with collaborators who bring new life experiences or skill sets to the table. We make shows for Halifax and for places far away, with the support of The Canada Council for the Arts, Arts Nova Scotia, and The Nova Scotia Department of Communities, Culture, Tourism and Heritage, and Halifax Culture and Community. Zuppa is a member of Theatre Nova Scotia and an affiliate member of the Professional Association of Canadian Theatres.</span></span></p> </div> <div id='comp-m9u4mxv8' class='Z_l5lU ku3DBC zQ9jDz qvSjx3 Vq6kJx comp-m9u4mxv8 wixui-rich-text' data-testid='richTextElement'> <h6 class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><strong><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'> CREDITS</span></strong></h6> <ul> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Ben Stone &#8211; director</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Stewart Legere &#8211; performer</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Ben Stone and Stewart Legere &#8211; playwrights</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Fundy Geological Museum, Regan Maloney &#8211; science consultant</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Stewart Legere &#8211; composer</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Christian Ludwig Hansen &#8211; projection design</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Stewart Legere &#8211; sound design</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Jess Lewis &#8211; lighting and set design</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Leesa Hamilton &#8211; costume and set design</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Bernie Francis &#8211; Mi&#8217;kmaw language consultant</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Sophie Schade &#8211; producer</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Mary Fay Coady &#8211; interim producer</span></span></li> <li class='font_2 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>Gaby Milner &#8211; FSPA student apprentice</span></span></li> </ul> </div> <div id='comp-m9u4mxv91' class='Z_l5lU ku3DBC zQ9jDz qvSjx3 Vq6kJx comp-m9u4mxv91 wixui-rich-text' data-testid='richTextElement'> <p class='font_8 wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='wixui-rich-text__text'><span class='color_36 wixui-rich-text__text'>“* The participation of Ben Stone is arranged by permission of Canadian Actors’ Equity Association under the provisions of the Dance•Opera•Theatre Policy.”</span></span></p> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <div id='i8e4vmc5' class='BaOVQ8 tz5f0K i8e4vmc5 wixui-rich-text' data-testid='richTextElement'> <p><strong>TICKETS:</strong><strong>  </strong></p> <ul> <li><strong>Adults: $40</strong></li> <li><strong>Youth: $10</strong></li> <li>HST Additional</li> </ul> </div> <div class='style__notes___25v7J'> <div class='main-title'> <div class='TitleBlock__TitleMetaDataContainer-sc-1nlhx7j-2 hWHMKr'> <ul> <li><em>Doors open 45 minutes before showtime.</em></li> <li><em>King’s Theatre is committed to accessibility. If price is a barrier to attending, please request a ‘Bursary Ticket’ at the Box Office.</em></li> <li><em>Tickets are not refundable for cash, but can be exchanged for credit with a minimum of 48 hours notice. Credits are valid for 12 months.</em></li> <li><em>All persons require a ticket; we do not allow babes in arms. Children under 12 must be accompanied by a guardian.</em></li> <li><em>Outside food and beverages may not be brought into the theatre.</em></li> <li><em>For more information about Theatre policies, click <a href='https://www.kingstheatre.ca/about/ticket-info/'>here.</a></em></li> </ul> </div> </div> </div> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> <p>&nbsp;</p> "
      }
    ],
